# Citation metadata for the arena as software and protocol. GitHub reads this
# file and offers "Cite this repository". The author is the team as a whole, the
# way community software is cited; people are credited on the papers, which will
# be added under preferred-citation when they are public, and in CONTRIBUTORS.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Social Simulation Arena, its protocol, or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Social Simulation Arena"
abstract: "A live benchmark for social simulation. Entrants forecast published population statistics before release; forecasts lock and are timestamped before the answer exists, and the released number scores them in public against a persistence baseline."
authors:
  - name: "Social Simulation Arena Team"
    website: "https://social-simulation-arena.com"
contact:
  - name: "Social Atoms"
    email: "hi@social-atoms.org"
    website: "https://social-atoms.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Social-Atoms/social-sim-arena"
url: "https://social-simulation-arena.com"
date-released: "2026-08-14"
version: "season-0"
keywords:
  - social simulation
  - forecasting benchmark
  - large language models
  - public opinion
  - computational social science
